<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berwyn range</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Berwyn Mountains</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Berwyn range is a range of moorland mountains in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, rising to 832 metres at Cadair Berwyn. In 1165 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> led a great army into Wales against a coalition of Welsh rulers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-gwynedd">Owain Gwynedd</a>, but storms and rain on the Berwyn forced him to retreat without a battle, and he took revenge by mutilating Welsh hostages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berwyn-range.jpg" alt="Berwyn range" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stemonitis at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cadair_Berwyn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
